  "body": "## What changed\nAfter the contributor's mm probe run on a 770MX (#521 / #583), PathPilot stayed in G21. LinuxCNC's `M2`/`M30` reset MDI mode, G54, G17, G90, G94, M48, G40, M5, G1 and M9, but **not the length unit** (LinuxCNC G-code reference, M-codes, \"M2, M30 Program End\").\n\nA new Tormach post option, **End in**, takes one of three values:\n- **Program's unit** (the default, byte-identical output);\n- **Inch (G20)**;\n- **mm (G21)**.\n\nWhen the choice differs from the program's unit, `G20`/`G21` is written on its own line after the final `G53 G0 Z0` / `G30` and right before `M30`, so no move is read in the new unit.\n- **Setting:** `PostOptions.end_units` (`EndUnits` in schema.rs), set through the existing undoable `SetPostOptions`.\n- **Project file:** an optional `post_options.end_units` key; a missing key means the default, so there is no version step. An unknown word refuses the file by name.\n- **Post page:** an \"End in\" row, shown only while Tormach PathPilot is the post.\n- **Other posts:** ignore it.\n- **Dropped, with reasons in `docs/decisions/596-end-native-units.md`:**\n  - a machine-file `native_unit` key, which would need a guess written into every stock file;\n  - a closing comment only;\n  - an on/off switch.\n\n## How tested\n- **New `tormach_end_units` (7):**\n  - the default writes no key, and the output is byte-identical;\n  - a mm program for an inch control ends `G53 G0 Z0 / G30 / G20 / M30`, and the G20 line is the only difference;\n  - an inch program for a mm control ends with G21;\n  - matching units add nothing;\n  - undo and redo;\n  - round-trip, including the unknown-word refusal.\n  - The two G20/G21 tests fail with the old .cps.\n- **UI:** `after_op_tests::end_units_choice_commits_and_undoes`.\n- **Gate:** tormach_post, tormach_machines, conformance (goldens unchanged), posting, program_entry, project_roundtrip, after_op, lathe_post_g76, per_op_files and all camcraft-post tests pass. Clippy (post/app/ui) is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\nA PathPilot Hub run with the option set.\n\nChangelog: Tormach post: new \"End in\" post option (default off) writes G20/G21 before M30, so a program can leave PathPilot in the operator's units (LinuxCNC's M30 does not reset G20/G21) (#596)\n\nFixes #596\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
